---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { articleNode } from '../lib/schema';
import { SITE_URL } from '../lib/site';

const title = 'Life Lessons from Kasra Dash';
const description =
  'Five life lessons from Kasra Dash in his own words: bar work, moving cities young, stepping out of the comfort zone, finding a mentor and choosing the five people around you.';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Life Lessons', href: '/life-lessons/' },
];

/* Kasra's own words (voice notes, 12 Aug 2026), structured into the numbered
 * format he chose. First person is deliberate on this page; the lessons run in
 * the order he learnt them, with no references. Grammar tidied lightly only —
 * the personality, including his blunter phrasing, is his and stays. */

const canonical = `${SITE_URL}/life-lessons/`;
const graphNodes = [
  articleNode({ canonical, headline: 'Life Lessons from Kasra Dash', description }),
];
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} path="/life-lessons/" breadcrumbs={crumbs} {graphNodes} type="article">
  <main>
    <section class="border-b border-tint-border bg-tint">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
        <Breadcrumbs {crumbs} />
        <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">Life Lessons from Kasra Dash</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Five lessons from my own path, in the order I learnt them. I am writing them down for other entrepreneurs, and maybe one day for kids who want to build something of their own.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
      <div class="reading-well prose prose-well max-w-3xl p-5 sm:p-8 lg:p-12">
        <h2>1. Work somewhere public facing</h2>
        <p>
          Everyone should work in a bar of some sort, somewhere properly public facing. You get to meet a lot of interesting characters, and you also come across a lot of, for lack of a better word, assholes. It is character building. You need to realise that everything in life does not run in straight lines. Sometimes the assholes are in person, sometimes they are keyboard warriors online, and sometimes they are trolls on YouTube.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Move to another city young</h2>
        <p>
          After I graduated university I moved from Scotland to Northampton. I literally did not know anyone. I moved because I needed a job. When you leave the city where all your mates and your family are, it pushes you out and forces you to become more outgoing.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Step out of your comfort zone</h2>
        <p>
          At eighteen or nineteen I got my very first web design client, and it was an e-commerce store. I had only ever touched brochure websites. I convinced the client anyway. The build took me about six months, and there was no AI at the time, this was around 2018. I earned about £5,000 from it, which was good money back then, especially for me.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Find a mentor</h2>
        <p>
          When I was nineteen or twenty I found James Dooley. He taught me a lot and fast-tracked my path, because he had already done the things I was trying to do, he knew the outcomes, and he guided me on the right path. If you do not want to go to university, find a mentor instead. A good mentor is worth its weight in gold.
        </p>

        <h2>5. You are the average of the five people you spend the most time with</h2>
        <p>
          People say they want to earn more, then hang around people who pull them down rather than drag them up. I was lucky. I picked five really successful people, and they pushed me to the next level. If your five friends all do six million a year and you do two, they can push you, because they know all of the downfalls and you can always ask them questions. And it is not just about money. Surround yourself with fitness people and they will push you in fitness too.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-tint-border bg-tint py-14">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 text-center sm:px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">More of the story</h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-xl text-muted">
          The longer version lives on the about page, and the conferences these years led to are on the speaking page.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
          <a href="/about-kasra-dash/" class="btn-gradient px-6 py-3 text-sm font-bold shadow-lg shadow-brand-500/25 transition hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-brand-500/40">
            About Kasra Dash
          </a>
          <a href="/speaking/" class="rounded-full border border-tint-border px-6 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-ink transition hover:border-brand-500 hover:bg-brand-500/10">
            Speaking
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
